  "notes": "The LAX flights are mostly ERJ-135s; drawn on the ERJ-145 (N861BB, 2026-09-24), the clearest side-on photo, and placed on the -135 by the landmarks. The bands' curve nearest the tail (royal behind it) is measured on N861BB; the three bands ahead of it are hidden by the wing there and are carried over from N11526 (2025-04-15) as distances ahead of that curve (about 1.0, 2.9 and 3.4 m), so where they meet the white is uncertain (low). The fin's faceting is simplified to its big fields: navy wedge, pale band, royal aft and lower forward, the mark's ring; the narrower navy and sky strips across the rudder and the sky facets either side of the mark are left in the sky base. 'CONTOUR' runs x 0.198-0.436 with its baseline at y -0.17 and its capitals about 1.2 m tall. The 'from' year is left out: no dated source in hand.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round (2026-11-20); Contour had no scheme here before."
}